Fall back to find_program() when pkg-config's wayland_scanner var is unusable

wx_protocols codegen (wxWidgets' vendored pointer-warp-v1 cursor support,
build/cmake/init.cmake:462-500) resolves wayland-scanner via
pkg_get_variable(WAYLAND_SCANNER wayland-scanner wayland_scanner). Under
this cross build that pc var resolves against the *target* sysroot's
wayland-scanner.pc (found via Buildroot's target pkg-config wrapper, which
is what everything else in this tree - gtk3, X11, wayland-client itself -
correctly resolves through). That .pc's `wayland_scanner` var is written
bare (${bindir}/wayland-scanner, no ${pc_sysrootdir} prefix, unlike
pkgdatadir a few lines above it in the same file), so it comes back as a
literal /usr/bin/wayland-scanner - a path on the build machine, not
anywhere in this tree.

Verified this is really what's happening, without executing anything
inside the build container (RUNPATH there is container-absolute, not
reproducible from outside it - confirmed unreliable the hard way first):
reproduced the same pkg-config variable lookup by hand against the
host-side mirror of xenia-edge's own per-package sysroot with
PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR/PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR set to match, and it printed
exactly /usr/bin/wayland-scanner.

`if(WAYLAND_SCANNER)` only checks the variable is a non-empty string, not
that the path exists, and none of the execute_process() calls that follow
pass RESULT_VARIABLE/ERROR_VARIABLE - so running a nonexistent (or
wrong-distro) /usr/bin/wayland-scanner fails completely silently at
configure time, and the only symptom is a much later hard compile error:
  wx/gtk/private/wayland.h:32:10: fatal error:
    'wx/protocols/pointer-warp-v1-client-protocol.h' file not found

The actual usable wayland-scanner is the one this package already builds
and stages at $(HOST_DIR)/bin/wayland-scanner (xenia-edge.mk's
BUILD_CMDS puts $(HOST_DIR)/bin first on PATH, and
002-cmake-find-root-path.patch already sets
CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PROGRAM=NEVER, so find_program() here searches
PATH instead of the target sysroot and lands on it). Make the pc-var path
a first choice but not the only one: fall back to find_program() when it
doesn't exist, and turn the truthiness check into an existence check so a
failed find_program() (empty result) can't silently fall through into the
same failure mode this patch exists to fix.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>

--- a/third_party/wxWidgets/build/cmake/init.cmake
+++ b/third_party/wxWidgets/build/cmake/init.cmake
@@ -466,7 +466,11 @@
                 pkg_check_modules(WAYLAND_CLIENT wayland-client)
                 if(WAYLAND_CLIENT_FOUND)
                     pkg_get_variable(WAYLAND_SCANNER wayland-scanner wayland_scanner)
-                    if(WAYLAND_SCANNER)
+                    if(NOT EXISTS "${WAYLAND_SCANNER}")
+                        find_program(wx_wayland_scanner NAMES wayland-scanner)
+                        set(WAYLAND_SCANNER "${wx_wayland_scanner}")
+                    endif()
+                    if(EXISTS "${WAYLAND_SCANNER}")
                         set(wx_protocols_input_dir ${wxSOURCE_DIR}/src/unix/protocols)
                         set(wx_protocols_temp_dir ${wxOUTPUT_DIR}/wx/protocols)
                         set(wx_protocols_output_dir ${wxSETUP_HEADER_PATH}/wx/protocols)
